      "description": "As a\n Shopper, \nI want \nproduct cards to display relevant information for the surface I am browsing, \nso that\n each page feels appropriately tailored without inconsistent component implementations across the site.\nImages for reference (Figma is leading):\nThis story covers the build of a single shared Product Card component that supports multiple display variations via a style prop. Each variation controls which elements are shown — the component itself is built and maintained once. The component is scoped to the visual and interactive layer only — product data is sourced from SFCC. \nVariations in scope: \nHomepage\nPLP\nWish List\nRecently Viewed",
