      "key": "SFCC-91",
      "summary": "PDP UI — Colour Swatches & Variation Selection",
      "description": "As a\n Shopper,\nI want\n to see all available colours for a product and be able to switch between them on the page,\nso that\n I can explore the full range of colour options before choosing which to buy.\nImage for reference (final design in Figma is leading):\nThis story covers the rendering of colour swatches on the PDP and the interaction logic when a shopper selects a different colour. Swatches are driven by the index image — one product image per colour variation that is designated in SFCC BM as the representative swatch image.\nMost products do not have a wide range of colours available, however, Dani confirmed max needed number of colours will likely be around\n 7. \nHere’s a current product that has 4 colours:\nLumi Sandal Lilac Online | Zimmermann",
      "status": {
