    {
      "id": "18141",
      "key": "SFCC-96",
      "summary": "Expanded Navigation (Desktop) - PWA Kit Component",
      "description": "As a\n Shopper,\nI want\n to see a mega menu appear when I hover over or click a top-level navigation category on desktop,\nso that\n I can quickly browse and navigate to subcategories and destinations without leaving the current page.\nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/380043284/Product+Category+Taxonomy\n \nReference Images (Figma is leading):\n\n\nContext:\nThe global header \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-746\n  displays a row of top-level navigation categories. On desktop, hovering over a category triggers a mega menu dropdown that displays the associated links and subcategories for that heading. The mega menu should feel immediate and responsive — it is the primary navigation mechanism for desktop shoppers.\nKey behaviours:\nHovering over a top-level nav item reveals the mega menu for that category\nThe mega menu displays the subcategory links and any associated content (e.g. campaign imagery, featured links);\nSub-category links -> driven by SFCC BM category taxonomy?\nEditorial campaign image → Contentful?\nThe mega menu remains open while the shopper's cursor is within either the triggering nav item or the open mega menu panel\nThe mega menu dismisses when the shopper's cursor leaves both the nav item and the mega menu panel boundary\nZ.Immerse is an exception — it functions as a direct link to a page and does not trigger a mega menu\nThe 'Back in Boutique' category is included in the nav and links to the relevant page without a mega menu\nNav items and their associated mega menu content are managed via the CMS; adding or removing items does not require a code change\nSub-category links -> driven by SFCC BM category taxonomy?\nEditorial campaign image → Contentful?\nThe global navigation structure is cloneable across markets to support regional storefronts\nThe mega menu is storefront-aware — sub-category links are driven by the catalogue configured in Business Manager for the active storefront, and the editorial image in the right panel is driven by the Contentful locale for the active storefront. This ensures regional variations in category structure and campaign imagery can be managed independently per storefront without a code change",
      "status": {
        "name": "To Do",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
      },
      "issue_type": {
        "name": "Story"
      },
      "priority": {
