        "Squad-B"
      ],
      "updated": "2026-08-14T16:50:29.874+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "18789",
      "key": "SFCC-428",
      "summary": "Global-e — Decide Optional Custom Hook Extension Points",
      "description": "As a\n Product Owner,\nI want\n a documented decision on which optional Global-e custom hook extension points Zimmermann needs,\nso that\n engineering knows exactly what custom code to build versus leave at OOTB default.\nThe vendor cartridge exposes ~20 optional custom hook extension points (marketing consent capture, cookie consent alignment, PLI metadata, backorder messaging, etc.) that currently all run on OOTB defaults with zero Zimmermann customization. Most are fine as-is, but a few (marketing consent, cookie consent) affect compliance and customer data capture and need an explicit decision rather than a default-by-omission. See the full checklist table in \ndocs/Global-e/main-config-gap-analysis.md\n, Customization/Hooks section.",
      "status": {
